{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Java and Python SDKs will be implemented as thin wrapper libraries over existing Fabric gRPC client APIs, following idiomatic language design patterns for each ecosystem to reduce development effort and ensure compatibility with existing Fabric network components.",
    "Pre-built user chaincode will be distributed as signed Docker images, with support for the three most common Fabric chaincode runtimes (Node.js, Java, Go) to cover the majority of use cases, leveraging the existing Fabric chaincode lifecycle for deployment and management.",
    "VSCC validation debug enhancements will be implemented by modifying the peer's txvalidator module to collect validation metadata during policy evaluation, with structured log output at the INFO level and optional event emission via the existing Fabric event hub to avoid introducing new infrastructure.",
    "Platform-specific tool binaries will be built using Go's native cross-compilation capabilities, targeting Linux (amd64, arm64), macOS (amd64, arm64), and Windows (amd64) to cover the most widely used developer and production environments, with all binaries signed using the project's existing release signing key.",
    "Certificate fingerprint validation will be implemented as a pluggable auth handler integrated into the peer endorsement flow, supporting two optional modes: fetching fingerprint lists from organization-controlled HTTPS endpoints at endorsement time, and validating against channel-configured signed fingerprint lists to accommodate different organizational trust requirements.",
    "Test network documentation will be integrated into the official Fabric documentation site, with links to existing test/ directory resources to avoid duplicating content, and will include step-by-step guides for both single-org and multi-org network deployment for testing use cases.",
    "Default configuration files will be extracted directly from the Fabric source code's hardcoded default values, organized into a new top-level config_defaults directory, with existing core.yaml, orderer.yaml, and configtx.yaml updated to reference these centralized defaults to ensure consistency."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The 'so I develop application with NodeJS' text in user stories U1 and U2 is assumed to be a copy-paste error, and the actual requirements are to provide standalone Java and Python SDKs for Fabric blockchain interaction, as the SDK type is explicitly specified in each user story.",
    "Existing Fabric core gRPC APIs, build pipelines, and event infrastructure are stable and do not require major refactoring to support the new features described in the user stories.",
    "The pre-built chaincode targets for U3 are limited to the three most common Fabric runtime environments (Node.js, Java, Go) as no additional runtime requirements are specified.",
    "The Java and Python SDKs (U1, U2) will only support Fabric v2.x and later features, with no requirement for backward compatibility with older Fabric versions.",
    "For U6, organization-controlled fingerprint list endpoints will use HTTPS with mandatory TLS certificate verification to prevent man-in-the-middle attacks, and signed fingerprint lists will be signed using the organization's existing MSP signing keys to avoid requiring new key infrastructure.",
    "All published tool binaries for U5 will be accompanied by SHA256 checksums to allow users to verify binary integrity after download.",
    "The default configuration extraction for U8 will only include configuration parameters that are actively used in the current Fabric release, with deprecated parameters excluded to avoid confusion.",
    "VSCC validation failure events for U4 will be emitted via the existing Fabric event hub, with no changes required to the core event infrastructure."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Development for Fabric Interaction",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a Java SDK wrapper for Fabric gRPC APIs, including core client functionality, transaction submission/query, event listening, unit tests, and basic usage documentation to enable Java developers to interact with Fabric blockchains.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Development for Fabric Interaction",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a Python SDK wrapper for Fabric gRPC APIs, following Python idiomatic patterns, including core client functionality, transaction submission/query, event listening, unit tests, and basic usage documentation to enable Python developers to interact with Fabric blockchains.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Pre-built User Chaincode Deployment Support",
      "activity_description": "Modify the Fabric peer chaincode lifecycle to accept pre-built signed Docker images as chaincode packages, update CLI tools (peer, configtxgen) to support pre-built chaincode deployment, test with Node.js, Java, and Go pre-built chaincode images, and document the deployment process for developers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 9
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "VSCC Validation Debug Logging and Failure Event Emission",
      "activity_description": "Modify the peer txvalidator module to capture policy details, signer peer/org names, and missing signers during VSCC validation, update log output to include this information at INFO level, add event emission for validation failures to the Fabric event hub, update Java and Python SDKs to expose these events, and document the new logging and event capabilities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Platform-specific Fabric Tool Binaries",
      "activity_description": "Update Fabric build scripts to support cross-compilation for Linux (amd64, arm64), macOS (amd64, arm64), and Windows (amd64), modify the release pipeline to build, sign, and publish binaries for all target platforms, test binaries on each platform for functionality, and update documentation with platform-specific download links and checksums.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Certificate Fingerprint Validation for Fabric CA",
      "activity_description": "Implement a pluggable auth handler for the peer endorsement flow to support optional certificate fingerprint validation, including support for fetching fingerprint lists from organization-controlled HTTPS endpoints and validating against channel-configured signed fingerprint lists with key rollover support, add configuration options for organizations, test with sample CA-issued certificates, and document the feature.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Test Network Quick Start Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Audit existing test/ directory resources, write step-by-step guides for spinning up single-org and multi-org test networks, create examples for testing custom chaincode frameworks with links to existing test READMEs, and update the official Fabric testing documentation page with the new content.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Centralized Default Configuration YAML Files",
      "activity_description": "Extract all default configuration values from Fabric source code for peer, orderer, configtx, and other components, organize them into a new config_defaults directory, update existing core.yaml, orderer.yaml, and configtx.yaml to reference the centralized defaults, update documentation and BYFN tutorials to link to the config_defaults directory, and verify completeness of all default configuration values.",
      "most_likely_effort": 9
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 76
  }
}

